<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad II of Córdoba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 980–1010</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Muhammad II al-Mahdi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad II al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdi">Mahdi</a> was an Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> who seized power in a revolt in February 1009, deposing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hisham-ii">Hisham II</a> and overthrowing the Amirid regime of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-sanchuelo">Sanchuelo</a>. His rule set off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fitna-of-al-andalus">Fitna of al-Andalus</a>: ousted by Sulayman with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> support later that year, he returned with Catalan help in 1010 but was killed within months.</p></div>
